{"openapi":"3.1.0","info":{"title":"Zevari Public API","version":"v1","summary":"REST API over Zevari's MCP-backed LinkedIn, campaign, lead, content, and agent capabilities.","description":"Zevari exposes an HTTPS JSON REST API described by an OpenAPI 3.1 contract. The production base URL is `https://api.zevari.ai`.\n\nThe API is built from the same public method contract used by Zevari's MCP-backed execution layer. Use the MCP reference when an AI assistant needs tool behavior, approval boundaries, or workflow semantics. Use this API reference when you need direct HTTP endpoints, schemas, request examples, and response shapes for a scheduled runner, CRM integration, internal tool, or agent bridge.\n\nTransport model: Zevari's public API uses endpoint-specific HTTP methods. Read operations use `GET` with query parameters. Create, action, approval, and generation operations use `POST` with a JSON body. Updates use `PATCH` with a JSON body. Deletes use `DELETE` with a JSON body when parameters are required.\n\nTo use the public API, you need a Zevari account, an active workspace subscription, and permission to the workspace and LinkedIn sender or workspace resource that backs the workflow. LinkedIn-backed actions depend on the connected sender account and Zevari's documented approval and safety behavior.\n\nApproval workflow for automated runners: create or update the workspace policy with `approvalPolicy.update` when an owner/admin wants hands-off execution. `mode: \"autopilot\"` with `autopilot_campaigns_enabled: true` (the legacy value `autopilot_expanded` still works and means the same) approves eligible low/medium-risk actions on its own, plus eligible campaign launches and enrollments of any size and action bundles of up to 20; the Safety Center still paces what reaches LinkedIn. It does not bypass safety, warm-up, high-risk/manual boundaries, InMail, standalone public posts, paid work, tainted data, deletes, exports, or account controls.\n\nFor a confirmation-gated REST write, call `confirmations.requestAction` with the exact executable payload first. If the response includes `data.autopilot.approved: true`, immediately call the write endpoint with the returned `confirmation_id`. If Autopilot is absent, false, or a policy or duplicate-withhold denial is returned, show or store `data.approval_url`, wait for the user to approve in Zevari, then retry the write endpoint with the same `confirmation_id`. REST clients should not call MCP-only chat approval tools.\nPersonalized campaign enrollment is the convenience exception: call `campaigns.addTargets` directly with each target's complete `personalized_steps` and a stable idempotency key. That call stages `campaign_enroll_personalized_targets` itself and either applies immediately under eligible Autopilot policy or returns the confirmation and exact retry guidance. After manual approval, repeat the exact request with `confirmation_id`.\n\nCampaign creation is a two-phase workflow. `campaigns.create` saves a draft. To launch it, stage `confirmations.requestAction` with `action_type: \"campaign_activate\"` and `payload: { \"campaign_id\": \"...\" }`, then call `campaigns.updateStatus` with `status: \"active\"` and the approved `confirmation_id`. Under Autopilot with campaign launches on (`autopilot` + `autopilot_campaigns_enabled: true`, legacy `autopilot_expanded`), eligible campaign activations of any size can come back already approved.\nCampaign enrollment is discoverable from runtime responses. `campaigns.create` returns `status`, effective `enrollment_mode`, `targets_editable`, `add_targets_method`, and `next_action`. Enrollment defaults to `fixed`; choose `continuous` when shared-copy additions should remain open. Active fixed and continuous campaigns both accept approval-bound per-target personalized sequences without pausing. Draft or paused additions remain unscheduled. Terminal campaigns are immutable, so create a new campaign instead.\n\nCreate API keys in the Zevari app at Dashboard Settings - API Keys. API keys start with `zvr_api_` and authenticate public API requests with `Authorization: Bearer <key>`. Keys are shown once, should be stored in a secret manager or environment variable, and should be rotated or revoked when access changes. Keep keys out of prompts, client-side code, CSV files, logs, and committed files.\n\nFor ordered REST call flows, read API Playbooks at `https://docs.zevari.ai/api/playbooks` before wiring automation. For manual, scheduled, and hybrid workflow design, read the Workflow Guide at `https://docs.zevari.ai/help/workflows`. For agent-facing tool semantics, read `https://docs.zevari.ai/mcp/reference`."},"servers":[{"url":"https://api.zevari.ai"}],"tags":[{"name":"agents"},{"name":"approvalPolicy"},{"name":"brandContext"},{"name":"brandPositioning"},{"name":"brandStories"},{"name":"campaignPlaybook"},{"name":"campaigns"},{"name":"confirmations"},{"name":"content"},{"name":"contentTemplates"},{"name":"inbox"},{"name":"leads"},{"name":"libraryContext"},{"name":"linkedin"},{"name":"outreachTemplates"},{"name":"profile"},{"name":"safety"},{"name":"settings"},{"name":"signals"},{"name":"skills"},{"name":"targets"},{"name":"voiceDna"}],"components":{"securitySchemes":{"bearerAuth":{"type":"http","scheme":"bearer","bearerFormat":"Zevari API key","description":"Use a Zevari API key created in dashboard settings. API keys start with zvr_api_."}},"schemas":{"ZevariError":{"type":"object","required":["code","message","docs_url","suggested_action"],"properties":{"code":{"type":"string","description":"Stable machine-readable error code.","examples":["invalid_arguments"]},"message":{"type":"string","description":"Human-readable error message."},"docs_url":{"type":"string","format":"uri","description":"Endpoint-specific documentation URL to review before retrying."},"suggested_action":{"type":"string","description":"Concrete recovery action for clients or agents."},"details":{"description":"Optional structured validation or execution details."}},"additionalProperties":false},"ZevariErrorEnvelope":{"type":"object","required":["error","request_id"],"properties":{"error":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ZevariError"},"request_id":{"type":"string","description":"Request correlation ID. Also returned in X-Zevari-Request-Id."}},"additionalProperties":false},"ZevariResponseEnvelope":{"type":"object","required":["ok","method","data","request_id"],"properties":{"ok":{"type":"boolean","description":"False when the underlying tool reports an error or a partial failure."},"method":{"type":"string","description":"Public API method name.","examples":["campaigns.delete"]},"data":{"description":"Parsed tool result. Shape is endpoint-specific."},"request_id":{"type":"string","description":"Request correlation ID. Also returned in X-Zevari-Request-Id."}},"additionalProperties":false}}},"paths":{"/v1/profile/get":{"get":{"tags":["profile"],"operationId":"profile_get","summary":"Get business profile","description":"Transport: call this endpoint with HTTP GET and query parameters. Get the current user's business profile: persona, company, ICP criteria, default CTA, and preferred tone. Read this before generating any outreach.","x-zevari-http-method":"GET","x-zevari-tool":"profile_get","x-zevari-method":{"method":"profile.get","http_method":"GET","namespace":"profile","operation":"get","path":"/v1/profile/get","api_version":"v1","tool_name":"profile_get","docs_url":"https://docs.zevari.ai/api/reference#profile-get","sensitive":false},"x-sensitive":false,"x-agent-guidance":"Validate arguments against this schema before calling. If the API returns a docs_url, read that endpoint section before retrying.","externalDocs":{"url":"https://docs.zevari.ai/api/reference#profile-get"},"security":[{"bearerAuth":[]}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Successful Zevari API response.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ZevariResponseEnvelope"},"examples":{"default":{"value":{"ok":true,"method":"profile.get","data":{},"request_id":"req_example"}}}}}},"400":{"description":"Invalid arguments or method execution error.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ZevariErrorEnvelope"},"examples":{"default":{"value":{"error":{"code":"invalid_arguments","message":"Invalid arguments for profile.get.","docs_url":"https://docs.zevari.ai/api/reference#profile-get","suggested_action":"Compare the request body to this endpoint's OpenAPI schema and retry with only documented parameters.","details":[{"code":"invalid_type","path":["example_field"],"message":"Required"}]},"request_id":"req_example"}}}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing, invalid, expired, revoked, or unauthorized API key.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ZevariErrorEnvelope"},"examples":{"default":{"value":{"error":{"code":"invalid_api_key","message":"The supplied Zevari API key is invalid, expired, revoked, or not authorized for this organization.","docs_url":"https://docs.zevari.ai/api/reference#profile-get","suggested_action":"Create a fresh Zevari API key for the target organization and LinkedIn sender, then retry."},"request_id":"req_example"}}}}}},"404":{"description":"Unknown or non-public Zevari API method.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ZevariErrorEnvelope"},"examples":{"default":{"value":{"error":{"code":"unknown_method","message":"Unknown Zevari API method: requested.method","docs_url":"https://docs.zevari.ai/api/reference#profile-get","suggested_action":"Fetch /v1/methods or /v1/openapi.json and retry with a documented endpoint."},"request_id":"req_example"}}}}}},"429":{"description":"API key rate limit exceeded.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ZevariErrorEnvelope"},"examples":{"default":{"value":{"error":{"code":"rate_limited","message":"API key rate limit exceeded.","docs_url":"https://docs.zevari.ai/api/reference#profile-get","suggested_action":"Wait for the current hourly API-key rate-limit window to reset, then retry."},"request_id":"req_example"}}}}}},"500":{"description":"Unhandled server error.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ZevariErrorEnvelope"},"examples":{"default":{"value":{"error":{"code":"api_handler_error","message":"Zevari API request failed while executing the method.","docs_url":"https://docs.zevari.ai/api/reference#profile-get","suggested_action":"Read the endpoint docs_url, verify the request body and active Zevari context, then retry."},"request_id":"req_example"}}}}}}},"parameters":[]}},"/v1/profile/update":{"patch":{"tags":["profile"],"operationId":"profile_update","summary":"Update business profile","description":"Transport: call this endpoint with HTTP PATCH and a JSON request body. Update the user's business profile. Required before agent tools will produce accurate results.","x-zevari-http-method":"PATCH","x-zevari-tool":"profile_update","x-zevari-method":{"method":"profile.update","http_method":"PATCH","namespace":"profile","operation":"update","path":"/v1/profile/update","api_version":"v1","tool_name":"profile_update","docs_url":"https://docs.zevari.ai/api/reference#profile-update","sensitive":false},"x-sensitive":false,"x-agent-guidance":"Validate arguments against this schema before calling. If the API returns a docs_url, read that endpoint section before retrying.","externalDocs":{"url":"https://docs.zevari.ai/api/reference#profile-update"},"security":[{"bearerAuth":[]}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Successful Zevari API response.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ZevariResponseEnvelope"},"examples":{"default":{"value":{"ok":true,"method":"profile.update","data":{},"request_id":"req_example"}}}}}},"400":{"description":"Invalid arguments or method execution error.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ZevariErrorEnvelope"},"examples":{"default":{"value":{"error":{"code":"invalid_arguments","message":"Invalid arguments for profile.update.","docs_url":"https://docs.zevari.ai/api/reference#profile-update","suggested_action":"Compare the request body to this endpoint's OpenAPI schema and retry with only documented parameters.","details":[{"code":"invalid_type","path":["example_field"],"message":"Required"}]},"request_id":"req_example"}}}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing, invalid, expired, revoked, or unauthorized API key.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ZevariErrorEnvelope"},"examples":{"default":{"value":{"error":{"code":"invalid_api_key","message":"The supplied Zevari API key is invalid, expired, revoked, or not authorized for this organization.","docs_url":"https://docs.zevari.ai/api/reference#profile-update","suggested_action":"Create a fresh Zevari API key for the target organization and LinkedIn sender, then retry."},"request_id":"req_example"}}}}}},"404":{"description":"Unknown or non-public Zevari API method.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ZevariErrorEnvelope"},"examples":{"default":{"value":{"error":{"code":"unknown_method","message":"Unknown Zevari API method: requested.method","docs_url":"https://docs.zevari.ai/api/reference#profile-update","suggested_action":"Fetch /v1/methods or /v1/openapi.json and retry with a documented endpoint."},"request_id":"req_example"}}}}}},"429":{"description":"API key rate limit exceeded.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ZevariErrorEnvelope"},"examples":{"default":{"value":{"error":{"code":"rate_limited","message":"API key rate limit exceeded.","docs_url":"https://docs.zevari.ai/api/reference#profile-update","suggested_action":"Wait for the current hourly API-key rate-limit window to reset, then retry."},"request_id":"req_example"}}}}}},"500":{"description":"Unhandled server error.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ZevariErrorEnvelope"},"examples":{"default":{"value":{"error":{"code":"api_handler_error","message":"Zevari API request failed while executing the method.","docs_url":"https://docs.zevari.ai/api/reference#profile-update","suggested_action":"Read the endpoint docs_url, verify the request body and active Zevari context, then retry."},"request_id":"req_example"}}}}}}},"requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"persona_type":{"type":"string","enum":["vc","saas_founder","recruiter","consultant","pe"],"nullable":true,"description":"User's persona type"},"full_name":{"type":"string","nullable":true},"job_title":{"type":"string","nullable":true},"company_name":{"type":"string","nullable":true},"company_description":{"type":"string","nullable":true},"product_offering":{"type":"string","nullable":true},"target_industry":{"type":"string","nullable":true,"description":"ICP: target industry"},"target_role":{"type":"string","nullable":true,"description":"ICP: target role/title"},"target_company_size":{"type":"string","nullable":true,"description":"ICP: target company size"},"target_company_revenue":{"type":"string","nullable":true,"description":"ICP: target company revenue"},"target_company_location":{"type":"string","nullable":true,"description":"ICP: target company location"},"min_icp_score":{"type":"number","minimum":1,"maximum":5,"nullable":true,"description":"Minimum ICP score (1-5) a sender needs before an inbox reply raises an alert. Does not change which leads count as Qualified (ICP agent score 4 or 5)."},"signal_keywords":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"nullable":true,"description":"Keywords for signal scanning (e.g. 'evaluating CRM', 'hiring sales team')"},"monitoring_topics":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"nullable":true,"description":"Topics for industry monitoring (e.g. 'AI in sales', 'outbound automation')"},"use_cases":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"nullable":true,"description":"Selected use cases"},"recommended_skills":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"nullable":true,"description":"Recommended skill slugs"},"default_cta_goal":{"type":"string","enum":["book_meeting","start_conversation","podcast_guest_invite","webinar_event_invite","free_audit_resource","get_published_pr","partnership_inquiry","feedback_review_request","other"],"nullable":true,"description":"Default CTA goal for outreach"},"default_cta_custom":{"type":"string","nullable":true,"description":"Custom CTA text when goal is 'other'"},"default_cta_resource_url":{"type":"string","nullable":true,"description":"Default resource URL for CTA (e.g., calendar link, landing page)"}},"additionalProperties":false},"examples":{"default":{"value":{"persona_type":"vc","full_name":"string"}}}}}}}},"/v1/voiceDna/save":{"post":{"tags":["voiceDna"],"operationId":"voiceDna_save","summary":"Save voice DNA","description":"Transport: call this endpoint with HTTP POST and a JSON request body. Save a user's writing style profile extracted from their own LinkedIn content.","x-zevari-http-method":"POST","x-zevari-tool":"voice_dna_save","x-zevari-method":{"method":"voiceDna.save","http_method":"POST","namespace":"voiceDna","operation":"save","path":"/v1/voiceDna/save","api_version":"v1","tool_name":"voice_dna_save","docs_url":"https://docs.zevari.ai/api/reference#voiceDna-save","sensitive":false},"x-sensitive":false,"x-agent-guidance":"Validate arguments against this schema before calling. If the API returns a docs_url, read that endpoint section before retrying.","externalDocs":{"url":"https://docs.zevari.ai/api/reference#voiceDna-save"},"security":[{"bearerAuth":[]}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Successful Zevari API response.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ZevariResponseEnvelope"},"examples":{"default":{"value":{"ok":true,"method":"voiceDna.save","data":{},"request_id":"req_example"}}}}}},"400":{"description":"Invalid arguments or method execution error.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ZevariErrorEnvelope"},"examples":{"default":{"value":{"error":{"code":"invalid_arguments","message":"Invalid arguments for voiceDna.save.","docs_url":"https://docs.zevari.ai/api/reference#voiceDna-save","suggested_action":"Compare the request body to this endpoint's OpenAPI schema and retry with only documented parameters.","details":[{"code":"invalid_type","path":["example_field"],"message":"Required"}]},"request_id":"req_example"}}}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing, invalid, expired, revoked, or unauthorized API key.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ZevariErrorEnvelope"},"examples":{"default":{"value":{"error":{"code":"invalid_api_key","message":"The supplied Zevari API key is invalid, expired, revoked, or not authorized for this organization.","docs_url":"https://docs.zevari.ai/api/reference#voiceDna-save","suggested_action":"Create a fresh Zevari API key for the target organization and LinkedIn sender, then retry."},"request_id":"req_example"}}}}}},"404":{"description":"Unknown or non-public Zevari API method.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ZevariErrorEnvelope"},"examples":{"default":{"value":{"error":{"code":"unknown_method","message":"Unknown Zevari API method: requested.method","docs_url":"https://docs.zevari.ai/api/reference#voiceDna-save","suggested_action":"Fetch /v1/methods or /v1/openapi.json and retry with a documented endpoint."},"request_id":"req_example"}}}}}},"429":{"description":"API key rate limit exceeded.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ZevariErrorEnvelope"},"examples":{"default":{"value":{"error":{"code":"rate_limited","message":"API key rate limit exceeded.","docs_url":"https://docs.zevari.ai/api/reference#voiceDna-save","suggested_action":"Wait for the current hourly API-key rate-limit window to reset, then retry."},"request_id":"req_example"}}}}}},"500":{"description":"Unhandled server error.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ZevariErrorEnvelope"},"examples":{"default":{"value":{"error":{"code":"api_handler_error","message":"Zevari API request failed while executing the method.","docs_url":"https://docs.zevari.ai/api/reference#voiceDna-save","suggested_action":"Read the endpoint docs_url, verify the request body and active Zevari context, then retry."},"request_id":"req_example"}}}}}}},"requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"style_system":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":{},"description":"Complete voice profile: syntax_patterns, vocabulary, tone, formatting, outreach_style"},"banned_words":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"description":"Words the user never uses"},"anti_voice":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"description":"3-5 phrases representing the opposite of how the user writes"},"killer_lines":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"description":"Exact lines the user wrote that are distinctive"},"samples_count":{"type":"number","description":"Number of writing samples analyzed"}},"required":["style_system"],"additionalProperties":false},"examples":{"default":{"value":{"style_system":{}}}}}}}}},"/v1/content/save":{"post":{"tags":["content"],"operationId":"content_save","summary":"Save content draft","description":"Transport: call this endpoint with HTTP POST and a JSON request body. Save a content draft (post, comment, message, sequence). For LinkedIn posts the user wants scheduled, save the draft here, then **stop and give the user the `dashboard_url` from the result** (https://zevari.ai/dashboard/content/{contentId}) — that page is where they review the post, upload an image or PDF, and pick a publish time. Media can also be attached through MCP: if the user uploaded a file in Settings > Media and gives you its ma_ id, call media_assets_attach; if they give a public HTTPS URL, call media_assets_attach_from_url. Do NOT call content_schedule yourself unless the user explicitly says they don't want to add media.","x-zevari-http-method":"POST","x-zevari-tool":"content_save","x-zevari-method":{"method":"content.save","http_method":"POST","namespace":"content","operation":"save","path":"/v1/content/save","api_version":"v1","tool_name":"content_save","docs_url":"https://docs.zevari.ai/api/reference#content-save","sensitive":false},"x-sensitive":false,"x-agent-guidance":"Validate arguments against this schema before calling. If the API returns a docs_url, read that endpoint section before retrying.","externalDocs":{"url":"https://docs.zevari.ai/api/reference#content-save"},"security":[{"bearerAuth":[]}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Successful Zevari API response.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ZevariResponseEnvelope"},"examples":{"default":{"value":{"ok":true,"method":"content.save","data":{},"request_id":"req_example"}}}}}},"400":{"description":"Invalid arguments or method execution error.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ZevariErrorEnvelope"},"examples":{"default":{"value":{"error":{"code":"invalid_arguments","message":"Invalid arguments for content.save.","docs_url":"https://docs.zevari.ai/api/reference#content-save","suggested_action":"Compare the request body to this endpoint's OpenAPI schema and retry with only documented parameters.","details":[{"code":"invalid_type","path":["example_field"],"message":"Required"}]},"request_id":"req_example"}}}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing, invalid, expired, revoked, or unauthorized API key.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ZevariErrorEnvelope"},"examples":{"default":{"value":{"error":{"code":"invalid_api_key","message":"The supplied Zevari API key is invalid, expired, revoked, or not authorized for this organization.","docs_url":"https://docs.zevari.ai/api/reference#content-save","suggested_action":"Create a fresh Zevari API key for the target organization and LinkedIn sender, then retry."},"request_id":"req_example"}}}}}},"404":{"description":"Unknown or non-public Zevari API method.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ZevariErrorEnvelope"},"examples":{"default":{"value":{"error":{"code":"unknown_method","message":"Unknown Zevari API method: requested.method","docs_url":"https://docs.zevari.ai/api/reference#content-save","suggested_action":"Fetch /v1/methods or /v1/openapi.json and retry with a documented endpoint."},"request_id":"req_example"}}}}}},"429":{"description":"API key rate limit exceeded.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ZevariErrorEnvelope"},"examples":{"default":{"value":{"error":{"code":"rate_limited","message":"API key rate limit exceeded.","docs_url":"https://docs.zevari.ai/api/reference#content-save","suggested_action":"Wait for the current hourly API-key rate-limit window to reset, then retry."},"request_id":"req_example"}}}}}},"500":{"description":"Unhandled server error.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ZevariErrorEnvelope"},"examples":{"default":{"value":{"error":{"code":"api_handler_error","message":"Zevari API request failed while executing the method.","docs_url":"https://docs.zevari.ai/api/reference#content-save","suggested_action":"Read the endpoint docs_url, verify the request body and active Zevari context, then retry."},"request_id":"req_example"}}}}}}},"requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"content_type":{"type":"string","enum":["post","comment","connection_note","message_sequence","lead_magnet","article","report"],"description":"Type of content"},"title":{"type":"string","description":"Content title (for lead magnets, articles)"},"body":{"type":"string","description":"The content text"},"skill_id":{"type":"string","description":"Skill that generated this content"},"campaign_id":{"type":"string","description":"Associated campaign ID"},"voice_dna_used":{"type":"boolean","default":false,"description":"Whether Voice DNA was applied"},"variants":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"label":{"type":"string"},"body":{"type":"string"}},"required":["label","body"],"additionalProperties":false},"description":"Alternative versions"},"metadata":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":{},"description":"Additional metadata"}},"required":["content_type","body"],"additionalProperties":false},"examples":{"default":{"value":{"content_type":"post","body":"string"}}}}}}}},"/v1/content/list":{"get":{"tags":["content"],"operationId":"content_list","summary":"List content drafts","description":"Transport: call this endpoint with HTTP GET and query parameters. List saved content drafts by type and status.","x-zevari-http-method":"GET","x-zevari-tool":"content_list","x-zevari-method":{"method":"content.list","http_method":"GET","namespace":"content","operation":"list","path":"/v1/content/list","api_version":"v1","tool_name":"content_list","docs_url":"https://docs.zevari.ai/api/reference#content-list","sensitive":false},"x-sensitive":false,"x-agent-guidance":"Validate arguments against this schema before calling. If the API returns a docs_url, read that endpoint section before retrying.","externalDocs":{"url":"https://docs.zevari.ai/api/reference#content-list"},"security":[{"bearerAuth":[]}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Successful Zevari API response.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ZevariResponseEnvelope"},"examples":{"default":{"value":{"ok":true,"method":"content.list","data":{},"request_id":"req_example"}}}}}},"400":{"description":"Invalid arguments or method execution error.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ZevariErrorEnvelope"},"examples":{"default":{"value":{"error":{"code":"invalid_arguments","message":"Invalid arguments for