rn the data.approval_url to the user, and wait for them to approve. Only then call this tool with the confirmation_id. Without it, this tool returns an error."},"bulk_item_id":{"type":"string","description":"Set when confirmation_id refers to a bulk_actions parent (from confirmations.requestAction). Identifies the per-item child to consume — e.g. 'itm_03'. Omit for single-action confirmations."}},"required":["postId"],"additionalProperties":false},"examples":{"default":{"value":{"postId":"example_id"}}}}}}}},"/v1/linkedin/commentOnPost":{"post":{"tags":["linkedin"],"operationId":"linkedin_commentOnPost","summary":"Comment on LinkedIn post","description":"Transport: call this endpoint with HTTP POST and a JSON request body. Post a comment on a LinkedIn post, or reply to an existing comment. REQUIRES confirmations.requestAction first. For postId, use the post's resolved social_id when available; Zevari resolves URL activity/share/ugcPost ids to social_id before approval. Public REST flow: first call confirmations.requestAction with the exact payload you intend to execute. If Autopilot returns approved=true, retry this endpoint immediately with confirmation_id. Otherwise wait for approval_url to be approved in Zevari, then retry with confirmation_id.","x-zevari-http-method":"POST","x-zevari-tool":"linkedin_comment_on_post","x-zevari-method":{"method":"linkedin.commentOnPost","http_method":"POST","namespace":"linkedin","operation":"commentOnPost","path":"/v1/linkedin/commentOnPost","api_version":"v1","tool_name":"linkedin_comment_on_post","docs_url":"https://docs.zevari.ai/api/reference#linkedin-commentOnPost","sensitive":true},"x-sensitive":true,"x-agent-guidance":"LinkedIn share, UGC post, and activity identifiers are not interchangeable. Resolve URLs with linkedin.getPost and use the returned social_id for write actions.","externalDocs":{"url":"https://docs.zevari.ai/api/reference#linkedin-commentOnPost"},"security":[{"bearerAuth":[]}],"responses":{"200":{"descriptio